Prj-BENCH — licensing
=====================

This repository is a MIXED-LICENCE COLLECTION. Read this file before reusing
any part of it.


1. The Prj-BENCH authors' own contributions
-------------------------------------------

SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0
Full licence text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

Copyright (c) 2026 the Prj-BENCH authors.

Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence.
This covers only the material we authored, namely:

  - everything under harness/ (the zero-shot inference code)
  - the quality-control layer: benchmarks/_manifest.csv,
    benchmarks/_dropped_items.csv, benchmarks/LICENSES.csv
  - the harmonised schema, the option sets and fixed question strings we wrote
    when recasting source tasks as multiple choice, and the QC decisions that
    define the curated release
  - this README and the figures in docs/


2. The benchmark data
---------------------

It does NOT cover the underlying benchmark items. Those remain under the
licences of their original sources and are redistributed here in modified form.
Each source has its own directory carrying its own LICENSE file:

  benchmarks/<release>/<source>/LICENSE

benchmarks/LICENSES.csv gives the same mapping in machine-readable form: which
benchmark comes from which source, under which SPDX identifier.

The collection spans Apache-2.0, MIT, CC BY 4.0, CC BY-SA 4.0, CC BY-NC 4.0 and
CC BY-NC 2.0. One further subset is not redistributed at all (section 4). There is no single
licence under which the whole collection may be redistributed, and the licence
on this file does not grant rights over the data.


3. Non-commercial subsets
-------------------------

Two benchmarks are NON-COMMERCIAL ONLY and may not be used for commercial
purposes under any circumstances:

  mhqa         MHQA           CC BY-NC 2.0
  medethicsqa  MedEthicsQA    CC BY-NC 4.0

Any commercial use of this repository must exclude those two benchmarks.
MedCalc is CC BY-SA 4.0, which additionally imposes a share-alike obligation on
adapted versions of that subset.


4. Subset that is NOT redistributed
-----------------------------------

medbullets (MedBullets) is part of the benchmark suite as analysed in the paper,
but its data file is NOT included in this repository.

No licence could be established: neither the Hugging Face mirror we drew from nor
the originating repository declares one, and the underlying questions derive from
a commercial medical question bank. Rather than redistribute items with no
permission behind them, the file is omitted and the source is linked instead.

benchmarks/<release>/medbullets/ retains a LICENSE explaining the omission and an
item_ids.csv listing the ids in each release, so the full suite can be rebuilt
from upstream. Identifiers are references, not content.


5. Attribution
--------------

The CC licences here require attribution and an indication of changes. Each
source directory's LICENSE file records what we modified. When reusing a subset,
cite the original dataset as well as this work; full citations for every source
are given in the accompanying paper.
